E["npc:agathelos-the-raging"] = {t="npc",n="Agathelos the Raging",z="razorfenkraul",s="Agathelos the Raging is a colossal armored boar penned within the thorned tunnels of Razorfen Kraul. Reared by the Death's Head quilboar as a living siege engine and avatar of their ancient god, he has been driven into a violent, unnatural frenzy. His sheer mass and strength make him one of the most dangerous beasts lurking under the Southern Barrens.",h="Agathelos the Raging is a colossal armored boar penned within the thorned tunnels of Razorfen Kraul.",sec={{t="Avatars of the Great Boar",b="Quilboar venerate all swine as descendants of their patron deity and progenitor, the god Agamaggan. To them, boars of exceptional size and tenacity are considered direct blessings from their fallen god. A beast the size of Agathelos—standing roughly twice as tall as a Barrens thunder lizard—carries massive spiritual and ceremonial significance among the Razorfen tribes.",sp=0},{t="A Weapon of the Death's Head",b="The Death's Head tribe, not content to leave Agathelos as merely a sacred icon, actively transformed him into a weapon of war. By force-feeding him the noxious bat guano gathered from the cavern ceilings of the Kraul, his handlers induced a maddened, unending delirium. The foul mixture drastically increased the colossal beast's stamina and fury, transforming him into a rampage waiting to be unleashed upon the tribe's rivals.",sp=0},{t="Kept in Chains",b="Because Agathelos is completely out of his mind with rage, even his handlers cannot let him roam loose within the Kraul. He is kept trapped in a dead-end tunnel behind an energetic ward maintained by quilboar shamans and guards. Should intruders break past the barrier, they face a beast driven completely wild by chemical madness, growing even more terrifying in size and power when struck.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is Agathelos so huge?",a="Agathelos is naturally a massive specimen of swine, which the quilboar revere as a divine blessing of Agamaggan. His unnatural bulk and swollen strength were further enhanced by the Death's Head tribe feeding him potent bat guano to induce a hulking, berserk state.",al={"why is agathelos big","agathelos size","giant boar barrens"}},{q="Why do the quilboar keep him locked behind a barrier?",a="The bat guano fed to Agathelos drove him completely insane with rage. Because he cannot tell friend from foe, his quilboar wardens must keep him sealed inside a fortified cul-de-sac using magical fields until they are ready to direct his wrath against their enemies.",al={"agathelos barrier","why is agathelos caged","agathelos force field"}},{q="What is his connection to Agamaggan?",a="Agamaggan is the great boar Ancient and progenitor of the quilboar race. Because of this ancestry, quilboar view all boars as sacred, and gigantic specimens like Agathelos are revered as living embodiments and divine gifts of Agamaggan's enduring bloodline.",al={"agathelos agamaggan","is agathelos a god","agamaggan son"}},{q="What tribe created Agathelos?",a="The Death's Head quilboar, the necromantic and fanatical caste embedded within the Razorfen, captured and cultivated Agathelos. They intended to unleash him as a living battering ram against anyone who challenges their dominion over the Barrens.",al={"who made agathelos","who feeds agathelos","agathelos tribe"}},{q="Why was he fed bat guano?",a="The guano produced by the bats nesting in Razorfen Kraul contains hallucinogenic and maddening properties. When fed to Agathelos, it acted as a stimulant that drastically heightened his stamina, aggression, and pain tolerance at the expense of his sanity.",al={"bat guano boar","why feed guano","kraul bat guano"}},{q="Can hunters tame Agathelos?",a="No. Agathelos is an elite, heavily armored monster whose rage is too deeply rooted in madness and dark sorcery to be brought under a hunter's control.",al={"tame agathelos","can i tame agathelos","hunter agathelos"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="A hunter can appreciate the sheer predatory bulk of Agathelos, though his twisted, chemically fueled madness marks him as a tragic perversion of natural beasts.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold Agamaggan in high esteem as one of the great Ancients who fell during the War of the Ancients; witnessing a sacred boar tortured with bat poison to serve as a siege weapon is an affront to Cenarius's wild balance.",["race:Tauren"]="The earth-attuned tauren know the legends of Agamaggan well, recognizing that the quilboar's corruption of his kindred beasts is another sign of the rot infesting the Barrens."},kw={"agamaggan","agathelos","boar","death's head","guano","quilboar","raging","razorfen kraul"},rel={"zone:razorfenkraul","topic:agamaggan","topic:quilboar","topic:razorfen"},src={"Agathelos the Raging"}}
E["npc:aggem-thorncurse"] = {t="npc",n="Aggem Thorncurse",z="razorfenkraul",s="Aggem Thorncurse is a spectral quilboar encountered deep within the thorned tunnels of Razorfen Kraul. Bound beyond death to the service of his tribe, he fights alongside Warlord Ramtusk and Death Speaker Jargba to defend their sacred redoubt against intruders.",h="Aggem Thorncurse is a spectral quilboar encountered deep within the thorned tunnels of Razorfen Kraul.",sec={{t="Guardian in Death",b="Within the heart of Razorfen Kraul, the quilboar fight desperately to protect their ancestral dens from outsiders. Aggem Thorncurse is not among the living defenders; instead, he lingers as a restless spirit. Bound to the physical realm by dark geomancy and shamanic rites, Aggem takes up arms when intruders threaten the tribe's warlord.",sp=0},{t="The Warlord's Entourage",b="Aggem does not battle alone. When outsiders challenge Warlord Ramtusk, Thorncurse manifests beside Death Speaker Jargba. Through potent mystical links, the spirits and flesh of these three defenders are bound together in combat, sharing the wounds dealt to them and proving that in Razorfen, loyalty to the tribe endures long past the grave.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Aggem Thorncurse?",a="Aggem Thorncurse is a spectral quilboar found in Razorfen Kraul. He appears alongside Death Speaker Jargba as one of the defenders accompanying Warlord Ramtusk.",al={"aggem thorncurse","who is aggem","aggem rf kraul"}},{q="Where can Aggem Thorncurse be found?",a="Aggem is encountered inside Razorfen Kraul, deep within the southern Barrens. He manifests directly in the chamber of Warlord Ramtusk when the chieftain is challenged.",al={"aggem location","where is aggem","where to find aggem thorncurse"}},{q="Why is Aggem a ghost?",a="Through the death magic and ancestral geomancy practiced by the Death's Head tribe and quilboar priests, powerful ancestors and fallen champions can be called back to defend the Kraul from invaders.",al={"why is he dead","why is aggem a spirit","ghost quilboar"}},{q="How does Aggem fight in combat?",a="Aggem fights in concert with Warlord Ramtusk and Death Speaker Jargba. Connected by potent shamanic magic like Spirit Link, damage inflicted upon him or his allies is shared across the trio, requiring attackers to weather their combined assault.",al={"aggem abilities","how does aggem fight","spirit link boss"}},{q="Is Aggem Thorncurse affiliated with a specific quilboar tribe?",a="He belongs to the Razorfen quilboar residing in the Kraul, fighting directly in defense of Warlord Ramtusk.",al={"aggem tribe","what tribe is aggem","razorfen quilboar"}},{q="Can you encounter Aggem Thorncurse outside of the Ramtusk fight?",a="No. Aggem Thorncurse is strictly bound to the Warlord Ramtusk encounter, manifesting alongside his warlord and fellow advisor when battle begins.",al={"aggem solo","can you fight aggem alone","aggem wandering"}}},ang={["class:Shaman"]="Seeing ancestral spirits chained to the mortal world through totems and geomantic rites is a potent display of raw quilboar spiritualism.",["class:Priest"]="The binding of spirits beyond the grave by the quilboar hints at dark necromantic practices taking root deep within Razorfen.",["faction:Horde"]="With the quilboar constantly menacing the Barrens, putting down persistent defenders like Aggem Thorncurse helps secure the lands of Durotar and Mulgore."},kw={"aggem","ghost","jargba","kraul","quilboar","ramtusk","razorfen","spirit link","thorncurse"},rel={"zone:razorfenkraul","topic:quilboar","topic:razorfen"},src={"Aggem Thorncurse"}}
E["npc:blind-hunter"] = {t="npc",n="Blind Hunter",z="razorfenkraul",s="The Blind Hunter is an elusive, albino bat that roosts deep within Razorfen Kraul. Unlike the ordinary bats nesting near the cavern entrances, this rare creature prowls the sunless depths of the quilboar redoubt.",h="The Blind Hunter is an elusive, albino bat that roosts deep within Razorfen Kraul.",sec={{t="Depths of the Kraul",b="Razorfen Kraul is riddled with winding briars and dark subterranean caverns. While common Kraul bats roost nearer to the surface where faint light filters in from the outside world, the Blind Hunter has adapted entirely to the furthest, darkest alcoves of the tangle. Its pale, albino hide and milky gaze are likely the result of generations spent completely isolated from natural sunlight.",sp=0},{t="A Rare Quarry",b="True to its name, scholars and scouts believe the creature has lost most or all of its conventional eyesight, relying instead on keen senses of hearing and echolocation to track prey through the gloom. It rarely shows itself, appearing only on occasion to hunt through the dense thickets, making an encounter with this phantom beast a prized occurrence among cavern explorers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Blind Hunter?",a="The Blind Hunter is a rare albino bat dwelling in the deepest, pitch-black tunnels of Razorfen Kraul. It is remarkably pale and elusive compared to the common cavern bats found closer to the entrance.",al={"who is blind hunter","what is blind hunter","blind hunter bat"}},{q="Where does the Blind Hunter appear?",a="It dwells in the shadowy interior paths of Razorfen Kraul, nesting well past the threshold where outside daylight fades away entirely.",al={"blind hunter location","where to find blind hunter","blind hunter spawn"}},{q="Is the Blind Hunter actually blind?",a="While naturalists and adventurers suspect it is truly blind due to its milky eyes and deep-cave habitat, its hunting ability remains razor-sharp, relying on keen hearing and echolocation in the darkness.",al={"is it blind","can blind hunter see"}},{q="Can hunters tame the Blind Hunter?",a="Yes, beastmasters capable of managing winged predators can tame the Blind Hunter, making it a distinctive pale companion for those patient enough to track it down.",al={"can i tame blind hunter","blind hunter tameable","blind hunter pet"}},{q="Why is the Blind Hunter white?",a="It is an albino specimen whose coloration likely developed from living in perpetual darkness far from the reach of the sun, unlike bats that venture near the cave mouth.",al={"why is it albino","why is blind hunter white","albino bat"}},{q="How does it differ from regular Kraul bats?",a="Ordinary Kraul bats possess typical dark coloration and live nearer to the entrance where light still penetrates, whereas the Blind Hunter is pale, reclusive, and adapted strictly to deep subterranean tunnels.",al={"kraul bat difference","kraul bat vs blind hunter"}}},ang={["class:Hunter"]="For beastmasters traversing the Barrens, the Blind Hunter represents a prize quarry—either as a rare albino beast to tame or as a source of well-crafted subterranean bows."},kw={"albino bat","blind hunter","kraul bat","kraul beast","rare bat","razorfen kraul"},rel={"zone:razorfenkraul","topic:razorfen","topic:light"},src={"Blind Hunter"}}
E["npc:charlga-razorflank"] = {t="npc",n="Charlga Razorflank",z="razorfenkraul",s="Charlga Razorflank, widely known as the Crone of the Kraul, is the fierce and cunning geomancer chieftain presiding over Razorfen Kraul. Under her leadership, the Razorfen quilboar drove the tauren out of the southern Barrens through ruthless expansion, claiming to fight in the name of their fallen god, Agamaggan.",h="Charlga Razorflank, widely known as the Crone of the Kraul, is the fierce and cunning geomancer chieftain...",sec={{t="The Crone of the Kraul",b="Within the tangled, massive brambles of Razorfen Kraul rules Charlga Razorflank. Revered by her people as a master geomancer whose experimental magic remains unmatched among quilboar, Charlga organized her fractious kin into a unified, lethal threat. She harnessed the primal earth and giant thorns sprouting from the demigod Agamaggan's remains, reshaping the labyrinthine Kraul into an impenetrable fortress.",sp=0},{t="Expansion and Betrayal",b="Charlga rallied the quilboar under the banner of reviving their fallen patron, the Ancient Boar Agamaggan. Claiming that spilled blood would resurrect their deity, she directed constant, violent incursions across the southern Barrens, ultimately driving the tauren from their traditional homelands. Yet her true ambition goes deeper: Charlga secretly entered negotiations with emissaries of the undead Scourge, trading her unsuspecting tribe's devotion for unnatural power and insidious alliances.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Charlga Razorflank?",a="Charlga Razorflank is the chieftain and supreme geomancer of the Razorfen quilboar tribe, making her lair deep within Razorfen Kraul in the southern Barrens.",al={"charlga lore","who is the crone of the kraul","razorfen boss"}},{q="What magic does Charlga use?",a="She is an exceptionally gifted geomancer who manipulates elemental earth, crystal magic, and the massive blood-brambles born from the demigod Agamaggan.",al={"charlga abilities","geomancer powers"}},{q="Why did the quilboar attack the tauren in the Barrens?",a="Under Charlga's leadership, the quilboar waged war to displace the tauren from the southern Barrens, claiming the conflict would gather the blood needed to revive their wild god Agamaggan.",al={"why do quilboar hate tauren","barrens war quilboar"}},{q="Is Charlga working with the Scourge?",a="Yes. While telling her tribe they fight only to awaken Agamaggan, Charlga has been secretly negotiating with agents of the Scourge, aligning her kin with the undead for greater power.",al={"charlga scourge connection","unholy alliance quilboar"},sp=1},{q="What is Charlga's connection to Razorfen Downs?",a="Charlga is renowned for shaping much of the colossal thorn dome that protects Razorfen Downs, using her profound geomantic craft to fortify both great quilboar redoubts.",al={"charlga downs","charlga razorfen downs"}},{q="Why does the Horde want her dead?",a="The tauren and their Horde allies view her as an immediate existential threat due to her relentless raids, her theft of their lands, and her dangerous dealings with dark forces.",al={"crone of the kraul quest","why kill charlga"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="Charlga's aggressive expansion drove your people out of their ancestral territories across the southern Barrens, making her defeat a matter of tribal survival and reclamation.",["class:Shaman"]="While Charlga commands potent geomantic arts, her twisting of the elements and unholy bargains with the undead represent a dark corruption of sacred primal traditions.",["faction:Horde"]="Neutralizing Charlga is critical to securing caravan routes and encampments across the southern Barrens from relentless quilboar war parties."},kw={"agamaggan","barrens","charlga","crone","geomancer","kraul","quilboar","razorflank"},rel={"zone:razorfenkraul","subzone:razorfen-downs-classic","topic:quilboar","topic:agamaggan","topic:scourge","topic:tauren","zone:barrens","quest:1101"},src={"Charlga Razorflank"}}
E["npc:heralath-fallowbrook"] = {t="npc",n="Heralath Fallowbrook",z="razorfenkraul",s="Heralath Fallowbrook is a dying night elf druid imprisoned deep within Razorfen Kraul. Dispatched to investigate the thorny corruption surrounding the remains of the Ancient Agamaggan, he was captured and brutalized by the Razorfen tribe. With his final breaths, he seeks to send word of his fate and a cherished pendant back to his wife in Darnassus.",h="Heralath Fallowbrook is a dying night elf druid imprisoned deep within Razorfen Kraul.",sec={{t="A Tragic Mission",b="Sent by his people to investigate the ancient boar god Agamaggan and the spreading briars choking the southern Barrens, Heralath Fallowbrook sought the root of Razorfen Kraul's corruption. Instead of unearthing answers, the night elf was taken prisoner by the quilboar. Locked in a squalid pen and relentlessly beaten, Heralath succumbed to severe wounds and raging fever. Before fading entirely, he shared what he knew with a fellow captive, the dwarf Henrig Lonebrow, urging him to warn the sentinel outpost at Thalanaar about the aggression stirred up by the quilboar crone Charlga Razorflank.",sp=0},{t="A Dying Wish",b="Though Lonebrow managed to escape, Heralath was far too weak to flee. Lingering at death's door within the tangled pens of the Kraul, the druid clings to consciousness only long enough to entreat passing adventurers. He asks not for rescue, but for his wife Treshala's pendant to be recovered from his captors and carried back to Darnassus, ensuring she learns of his fate and knows he held her memory to the end.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Heralath Fallowbrook?",a="Heralath Fallowbrook is a night elf druid held captive inside Razorfen Kraul. He traveled to the Barrens to study the corruption of the brambles and the legacy of the fallen boar Ancient Agamaggan, but was captured and fatally tortured by the quilboar.",al={"who is heralath","heralath fallowbrook","night elf in razorfen"}},{q="What happened to Heralath inside Razorfen Kraul?",a="After being taken prisoner by the Razorfen quilboar, Heralath was beaten and locked in a hut. Between relentless abuse and illness, his body failed him, leaving him near death by the time rescuers could reach him.",al={"why is heralath dying","what happened to heralath fallowbrook"}},{q="What does Heralath ask travelers to do?",a="Knowing he will not survive, Heralath begs adventurers to recover his wife's pendant from the quilboar and bring it to her in Darnassus, bearing the tragic news of his death.",al={"heralath quest","mortality wanes quest"}},{q="Who was Henrig Lonebrow to Heralath?",a="Henrig Lonebrow was a dwarf captive held in the same pen as Heralath. Before Henrig managed to escape, Heralath shared vital information about Agamaggan with him and pleaded that word be delivered to the outpost of Thalanaar about Charlga Razorflank's movements.",al={"henrig lonebrow heralath","dwarf captive razorfen"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Seeing a fellow druid broken by the savage brambles of Razorfen Kraul is a stark reminder of the wild, unyielding corruption spreading unchecked through the southern Barrens.",["race:NightElf"]="Carrying Heralath's pendant back to Darnassus honors a fallen brother who gave his life attempting to understand and heal the wounded lands of Kalimdor."},kw={"agamaggan","fallowbrook","henrig lonebrow","heralath","mortality wanes","quilboar","razorfen kraul","treshala"},rel={"quest:1142","npc:treshala-fallowbrook","zone:razorfenkraul","quest:1100","topic:agamaggan","npc:charlga-razorflank","subzone:thalanaar","zone:darnassus"},src={"Heralath Fallowbrook"}}
E["npc:overlord-ramtusk"] = {t="npc",n="Overlord Ramtusk",z="razorfenkraul",s="Overlord Ramtusk is the grizzled commander of the Death's Head tribe's military forces deep within Razorfen Kraul. A massive, aging quilboar warrior, his hide is heavily scarred from decades of brutal clashes across the Barrens. Striking him down shatters the martial backbone of the Kraul's defenders.",h="Overlord Ramtusk is the grizzled commander of the Death's Head tribe's military forces deep within Razorfen...",sec={{t="Veteran of the Barrens",b="Overlord Ramtusk has survived decades in one of Kalimdor's most violent frontiers. His thick, leathery hide is crisscrossed with deep scars earned in skirmishes against centaur raiding parties, feral harpies, encroaching orcs, and stalwart tauren braves. While advanced age slows many warriors, Ramtusk's seasoned instincts and physical resilience have only hardened, allowing him to rule Razorfen Kraul's standing garrison with unyielding authority.",sp=0},{t="Commander of the Death's Head",b="Within the winding brambles of the Kraul, Ramtusk directs the military forces of the Death's Head quilboar. As their warlord, he maintains tight discipline among the bristled fighters defending the tribe's sanctum. Flanked by elite marksmen, Ramtusk fights like a frontline berserker, bellowing rallying shouts and unleashing earth-shattering slams that can break opposing battle lines in seconds.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Overlord Ramtusk?",a="Overlord Ramtusk is the supreme military commander of the Death's Head quilboar in Razorfen Kraul. He is an imposing, heavily scarred veteran who has fought every major power in the Barrens.",al={"who is ramtusk","ramtusk lore","overlord ramtusk"}},{q="Where can Overlord Ramtusk be found?",a="He commands his elite guards from within the thorny heart of Razorfen Kraul, located at the southern tip of the Barrens.",al={"ramtusk location","where is ramtusk","overlord ramtusk map"}},{q="What enemies has Ramtusk fought in the past?",a="His scarred hide tells the tale of countless clashes across the Barrens against centaur packs, territorial harpies, newly arrived orcs, and native tauren defenders.",al={"ramtusk enemies","who gave ramtusk scars","ramtusk battle history"}},{q="What tribe does Ramtusk belong to?",a="He is the high military leader of the Death's Head tribe, the dominant quilboar faction entrenched within Razorfen Kraul.",al={"ramtusk faction","ramtusk tribe","what quilboar tribe is ramtusk"}},{q="Why is Ramtusk targeted by adventurers?",a="As the supreme commander of the Death's Head forces, Ramtusk's death deals a crippling blow to the quilboar military hierarchy, throwing their defensive line into complete disarray.",al={"why kill ramtusk","take them down quest","ramtusk bounty"}},{q="How does Ramtusk fight?",a="Ramtusk fights as a classic battle-hardened warrior, using demoralizing cries to empower his cohort, crushing shockwaves to stagger enemies, and coordinating alongside elite ranged bodyguards.",al={"ramtusk tactics","ramtusk combat style","ramtusk abilities"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For generations, the nomadic tribes of the Barrens fought bitter skirmishes against Ramtusk and his marauders; putting him down avenges fallen braves.",["race:Orc"]="The quilboar have actively raided Horde settlements since the founding of Durotar and the Barrens outposts. Breaking Ramtusk's military command secures the Southern Barrens.",["class:Warrior"]="Ramtusk represents pure, brutal martial veteranhood, relying on thunderous strikes and commanding battle shouts rather than shamans' geomancy or thorn magic."},kw={"barrens","deaths head","overlord ramtusk","quilboar","ramtusk","razorfen kraul"},rel={"zone:razorfenkraul","topic:quilboar","topic:tauren","topic:centaur"},src={"Overlord Ramtusk"}}
E["npc:treshala-fallowbrook"] = {t="npc",n="Treshala Fallowbrook",z="razorfenkraul",s="Treshala Fallowbrook is a night elf residing quietly on the upper level of the Tradesmen's Terrace in Darnassus. Her attention is fixed upon the harsh, newly discovered vulnerabilities of mortal life following the Third War, leading her to study relics drawn from dangerous corners of Kalimdor.",h="Treshala Fallowbrook is a night elf residing quietly on the upper level of the Tradesmen's Terrace in...",sec={{t="A Watcher on the Terrace",b="Treshala Fallowbrook keeps a modest vigil on the second floor of a workshop in Darnassus's Tradesmen's Terrace. Like many of the kaldorei coming to terms with the sacrifice of their ancient immortality at Mount Hyjal, she observes the frailty that now stalks her people. She is closely tied to investigations into strange artifacts of power and survival—specifically interested in relics recovered from the brambled depths of Razorfen Kraul in the Barrens, seeking insight into how life endures or fades when its natural vigor begins to wane.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Treshala Fallowbrook?",a="She is located on the second floor of a workshop in the Tradesmen's Terrace of Darnassus. You can reach her room by heading up the wooden interior ramp inside the weapons building.",al={"treshala location","where is fallowbrook","how to find treshala"}},{q="What is Treshala researching?",a="Treshala studies the shift toward mortal vulnerability facing the night elves after the loss of the World Tree Nordrassil. She takes an active interest in artifacts of enduring vitality recovered by Alliance adventurers, including pendants retrieved from the hostile quilboar strongholds of Razorfen Kraul.",al={"treshala quest","mortality wanes lore","what does treshala want"}},{q="Why is she concerned with Razorfen Kraul?",a="Razorfen Kraul harbors foul magic and resilient thorny brambles rooted in the legacy of the boar god Agamaggan. Items uncovered within its depths, such as pendants of enduring vigor, offer curious scholars like Treshala insights into unnatural stamina and mortal preservation.",al={"why razorfen kraul","fallowbrook razorfen","connection to rfk"}},{q="Is she a shopkeeper or a craftswoman?",a="No, Treshala is neither a merchant nor a crafter. She resides above the busy artisan stalls of the Tradesmen's Terrace as an observant scholar concerned with the state of the kaldorei.",al={"is treshala a vendor","what does she sell"}}},ang={["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Treshala's concerns strike directly at the core of their post-Hyjal reality: the loss of eternal youth and the bitter necessity of facing true aging and disease.",["faction:Alliance"]="Treshala serves as an Alliance point of contact in Darnassus for champions returning from harrowing expeditions against the quilboar thorn-dens deep in the Barrens."},kw={"darnassus","fallowbrook","mortality wanes","night elf","razorfen kraul","tradesmen's terrace","treshala"},rel={"quest:1142","subzone:tradesmen-s-terrace","zone:darnassus","zone:razorfenkraul","topic:night-elf","quest:940"},src={"Treshala Fallowbrook"}}
E["quest:1101"] = {t="quest",n="The Crone of the Kraul",z="razorfenkraul",s="The Crone of the Kraul is an Alliance quest offered by Falfindel Waywarder at Thalanaar, on the border of Feralas and the Thousand Needles. After reading the recovered journal of the fallen dwarf Henrig Lonebrow, Falfindel tasks adventurers with infiltrating Razorfen Kraul and slaying the quillboar crone, Charlga Razorflank.",h="The Crone of the Kraul is an Alliance quest offered by Falfindel Waywarder at Thalanaar, on the border of...",sec={{t="A Plea at the Border",b="At the secluded night elf outpost of Thalanaar, Falfindel Waywarder grieves the loss of his scout Heralath and the dwarf Henrig Lonebrow. Lonebrow ventured deep into the Barrens to scout the quillboar hives but fell in battle, leaving behind a tattered journal detailing the growing menace within Razorfen Kraul. Realizing there is no time to send a runner to Darnassus for military reinforcements, Falfindel turns to passing adventurers to strike directly at the heart of the thorned dens.",sp=0},{t="Striking the Chieftain",b="The target of the expedition is Charlga Razorflank, an ancient geomancer and ruthless matriarch who has united the fractious Razormane tribes under her iron rule. From the depths of the Kraul, she marshals a bristling army that threatens neighboring lands. Adventurers must carve through thick thorn mazes, battlement walls, and swarms of fanatical quillboar warriors to corner Charlga and pry her medallion from her lifeless body as proof of her downfall.",sp=0},{t="A Deeper Corruption",b="While Charlga's demise blunts the immediate quillboar threat, her defeat raises deeper concerns for the night elves. The Kraul is formed from the living briars that sprouted where the boar Ancient, Agamaggan, fell during the War of the Ancients. When the medallion is returned, Falfindel notes that neutralizing Charlga allows night elf scholars to study the area's corruption more closely, though he senses that insidious treachery may be at the root of the sudden blight sweeping Agamaggan's sacred remains.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who gives the quest The Crone of the Kraul?",a="The quest is given by Falfindel Waywarder, a night elf stationed at Thalanaar. Thalanaar is an Alliance outpost located on the high mountain pass between Feralas and the Thousand Needles.",al={"quest giver crone of the kraul","where do i get crone of the kraul","falfindel waywarder quest"}},{q="What prerequisite must be completed before starting this quest?",a="You must first complete the quest Lonebrow's Journal. That task involves retrieving the journal of Henrig Lonebrow from his fallen remains near the entrance of Razorfen Kraul and delivering it to Falfindel in Thalanaar.",al={"prereq for crone of the kraul","how to unlock crone of the kraul","lonebrow journal prerequisite"}},{q="Who is Charlga Razorflank?",a="Charlga Razorflank is the supreme crone and matriarch of the Razorfen quillboar. She is a powerful geomancer who has united the warring tribes within Razorfen Kraul, directing their aggression against neighboring territories.",al={"who is the crone","charlga lore","charlga razorflank"}},{q="Where can Charlga Razorflank be found?",a="She resides at the very end of Razorfen Kraul, situated in the far southern corner of the Barrens near the Great Lift. She waits atop an altar deep inside the dungeon.",al={"where is charlga","charlga location","where is the crone in rfk"}},{q="Why does Falfindel need adventurers instead of calling the Darnassus army?",a="Thalanaar is a remote frontier outpost far from northern Kalimdor. With Charlga actively amassing her forces, sending word to Darnassus and waiting for a dispatched army would take too long to avert the rising danger.",al={"why not call darnassus","why hire adventurers"}},{q="What proof does Falfindel demand of the crone's death?",a="Falfindel requires Razorflank's Medallion, an amulet worn by Charlga herself that serves as indisputable evidence that the crone has been slain.",al={"what item drops","proof of demise item","razorflank medallion"}}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="This quest represents the primary Alliance initiative against the quillboar menace in the southern Barrens, launched from the outpost of Thalanaar.",["race:NightElf"]="Night elves view the desecration of Agamaggan's resting place with dismay, recognizing the boar Ancient as a fallen ally from the War of the Ancients.",["race:Dwarf"]="Avenging the explorer Henrig Lonebrow gives dwarves a personal stake in storming the quillboar stronghold.",["class:Druid"]="Druids hold Agamaggan in high esteem as a revered Ancient of nature and seek to cleanse the dark taint distorting his thorn-covered legacy."},kw={"agamaggan","charlga razorflank","crone","falfindel waywarder","lonebrow","medallion","razorfen kraul","thalanaar"},rel={"npc:charlga-razorflank","npc:falfindel-waywarder","quest:1100","zone:razorfenkraul","subzone:thalanaar","topic:agamaggan","topic:razorfen","zone:darnassus"},m={start="Falfindel Waywarder",level="27",faction="Alliance",id=1101},src={"The Crone of the Kraul"}}
E["quest:1142"] = {t="quest",n="Mortality Wanes",z="razorfenkraul",s="Deep within the hostile briars of Razorfen Kraul, a dying night elf named Heralath Fallowbrook whispers his final plea to passing Alliance adventurers. Stripped of his strength and life, he asks only that his wife's stolen pendant of bonding be recovered and brought home to Darnassus alongside news of his demise.",h="Deep within the hostile briars of Razorfen Kraul, a dying night elf named Heralath Fallowbrook whispers his...",sec={{t="A Dying Breath in the Thorns",b="Razorfen Kraul is a perilous redoubt overrun by savage quilboar and dark magic, far from Alliance territory. Among these treacherous brambles lies Heralath Fallowbrook, mortally wounded and fading fast. With his dying strength, he manages only broken whispers, revealing that a brave dwarf named Lonebrow was sent ahead to deliver a warning to Falfindel. Heralath, however, knows he will never leave the Kraul alive.",sp=0},{t="The Pendant of Bonding",b="Before succumbing to his wounds, Heralath clings to one final wish: retrieving a token of his marriage. A pendant symbolizing his eternal bond with his wife, Treshala, was torn from him by one of the lair's foul aggressors. He begs any traveler who stops beside him to recover the pendant and carry it all the way across Kalimdor to Darnassus, ensuring Treshala learns the truth of his lonely death rather than waiting in vain.",sp=0},{t="Grief in Darnassus",b="When Treshala Fallowbrook receives the recovered heirloom in Darnassus, she is devastated by the confirmation of her husband's demise. Confronting the harsh cruelty of the world, she vows that Heralath's work will not perish alongside him. Left to mourn in quiet solitude, she takes up the weight of his legacy while grappling with her sudden grief.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Heralath Fallowbrook?",a="Heralath Fallowbrook is an Alliance night elf found mortally wounded within Razorfen Kraul. Fading quickly from his injuries, he entrusts passing adventurers with recovering his wife's stolen bonding pendant and bringing news of his death to Darnassus.",al={"heralath fallowbrook","who is heralath","dying elf razorfen"}},{q="Where is Heralath Fallowbrook located?",a="Heralath is located inside Razorfen Kraul, the thorn-choked quilboar bastion situated in the southern reaches of the Barrens.",al={"heralath location","where is heralath","where to find heralath"}},{q="Who was Lonebrow?",a="Lonebrow is a brave dwarf mentioned by Heralath in his final moments. Lonebrow was apparently sent on an urgent errand out of the briars to warn Falfindel about the dangers unfolding in the Kraul.",al={"dwarf lonebrow","who is lonebrow","lonebrow warning"}},{q="Who is Treshala Fallowbrook?",a="Treshala is Heralath's wife, residing in the night elven capital of Darnassus. She receives the recovered pendant and must bear the tragic news of her husband's death.",al={"treshala fallowbrook","who is treshala","heralath wife"}},{q="What is the pendant of bonding?",a="The pendant of bonding is a cherished keepsake signifying the marriage between Heralath and Treshala Fallowbrook. It was stolen from Heralath by the quilboar aggressors in Razorfen Kraul before he died.",al={"treshalas pendant","what is the pendant","pendant of bonding"}},{q="How does Treshala react to the news?",a="Treshala is heartbroken by the tragedy and laments the cruelty of the world. Despite her profound grief, she resolves that Heralath's work must continue through her, asking to be left alone to mourn.",al={"treshala reaction","what happens when you deliver the pendant"},sp=1}},ang={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance champions venturing into the heart of the Horde-dominated Barrens, carrying Heralath's final token home to Darnassus is a somber duty of honor.",["race:NightElf"]="Night elves feel a deep personal sting seeing one of their kin perish alone and forgotten in the barbaric thistles of the southern Barrens.",["race:Dwarf"]="Heralath's dying words honor the bravery of the dwarf Lonebrow, who risked his life to carry an urgent warning away from the quilboar stronghold."},kw={"darnassus","falfindel","heralath fallowbrook","lonebrow","mortality wanes","pendant of bonding","razorfen kraul","treshala fallowbrook"},rel={"npc:heralath-fallowbrook","npc:treshala-fallowbrook","zone:razorfenkraul","zone:darnassus","topic:dwarf"},m={start="Heralath Fallowbrook",["end"]="Treshala Fallowbrook",level="30",faction="Alliance",id=1142},src={"Mortality Wanes"}}
E["quest:1221"] = {t="quest",n="Blueleaf Tubers",z="razorfenkraul",s="Blueleaf Tubers is a retrieval contract commissioned by the goblin merchant Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet. Seeking to profit from a rare subterranean delicacy, Mizzyrix equips adventurers with trained snufflenose gophers to locate and dig up the tubers buried inside the thorned depths of Razorfen Kraul.",h="Blueleaf Tubers is a retrieval contract commissioned by the goblin merchant Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.",sec={{t="A Prized Subterranean Delicacy",b="Blueleaf tubers are coveted across the world as a rare and lavish culinary delicacy. Despite their high value, harvesting them is notoriously difficult because they do not grow in open fields or standard wild groves. Instead, they are found almost exclusively deep in the sunless earth beneath the southern Barrens, tangled among the labyrinthine roots of Razorfen Kraul.",sp=0},{t="Mizzyrix's Ingenuity",b="Because the tubers remain completely buried and virtually impossible for ordinary humanoids to spot, the Ratchet merchant Mebok Mizzyrix devised an unusual solution. By training native snufflenose gophers—creatures capable of catching the scent of a buried tuber from fifty paces away—Mizzyrix turned vermin into foraging tools. He supplies scavengers with a command stick, a ventilated crate, and an instruction manual to guide the creatures through quillboar territory.",sp=0},{t="Harvesting in the Thorns",b="Reclaiming the tubers requires delving into the territory of the hostile Death's Head quillboar tribe. Foragers must protect their trained gophers from the feral beasts and thorny briars of the Kraul, commanding the rodents to unearth the hidden bulbs before packing them away for transport back to Ratchet, where Mizzyrix's high-paying foreign buyers await.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What are Blueleaf Tubers used for?",a="They are considered a rare and highly sought-after culinary delicacy around the world. Wealthy buyers pay significant sums for fresh tubers, making them a lucrative trade commodity for goblins like Mebok Mizzyrix.",al={"blueleaf tuber use","what are blueleaf tubers","why collect blueleaf tubers"}},{q="Where are Blueleaf Tubers found?",a="They grow buried in the subterranean earth and thorny root systems beneath the southern Barrens, specifically inside the quillboar stronghold of Razorfen Kraul.",al={"where to find blueleaf tubers","blueleaf tubers location","where do they grow"}},{q="Why do you need a Snufflenose Gopher to find them?",a="The tubers are hidden entirely underground and cannot be spotted with ordinary eyesight. The snufflenose gopher has a keen sense of smell that can detect buried tubers from up to fifty paces away, allowing it to dig them out of the dirt.",al={"why use gophers","snufflenose gopher purpose","how do gophers find tubers"}},{q="Who is Mebok Mizzyrix?",a="Mebok Mizzyrix is an entrepreneurial goblin merchant operating out of the neutral port town of Ratchet in the Barrens. He specializes in training native wildlife and acquiring exotic goods for foreign trade.",al={"who gives blueleaf tubers quest","mebok mizzyrix lore","ratchet goblin questgiver"}},{q="What equipment does Mizzyrix provide for the job?",a="Mizzyrix gives adventurers a Crate with Holes containing a trained gopher, a Snufflenose Command Stick used to direct the animal to dig, and a Snufflenose Owner's Manual outlining how to operate the beast.",al={"tuber quest items","gopher command stick","crate with holes"}},{q="Why can't Mebok gather the tubers himself?",a="Razorfen Kraul is heavily guarded by aggressive quillboar tribes, thorny vines, and dangerous subterranean predators. Mizzyrix prefers risking mercenary lives over venturing into the dangerous barrows himself.",al={"why doesnt mebok get them","why hire adventurers"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Culinary artisans know that blueleaf tubers are regarded as one of the rarest delicacies across Azeroth, fetched by elite buyers who prize their distinct, earthy flavor.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Unlike standard surface flora, blueleaf tubers thrive strictly underground amidst the briar roots of Razorfen, shielded from sunlight.",["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance expeditions entering the neutral port of Ratchet can take advantage of Mizzyrix's trade contract to justify a delve into hostile Horde-adjacent territory.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde warriors defending the Barrens from quillboar incursions can easily turn a profit on the side by running Mizzyrix's trained gophers through the Kraul."},kw={"blueleaf tubers","command stick","delicacy","mebok mizzyrix","quillboar","ratchet","razorfen kraul","snufflenose gopher","the barrens"},rel={"npc:mebok-mizzyrix","zone:razorfenkraul","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens","topic:razorfen","topic:goblin"},m={start="Mebok Mizzyrix",level="26",id=1221},src={"Blueleaf Tubers"}}
E["zone:razorfenkraul"] = {t="dungeon",n="Razorfen Kraul",z="razorfenkraul",s="Tucked away in the far south of the Barrens, Razorfen Kraul is the ancestral heartland of Kalimdor's quilboar. These ferocious tribes revere the dense labyrinth of giant brambles as the sacred resting place of their progenitor, the fallen demigod Agamaggan. Today, the Kraul has grown aggressively hostile under the tyranny of the quilboar matriarch Charlga Razorflank, whose dark dealings threaten the entire region.",h="Tucked away in the far south of the Barrens, Razorfen Kraul is the ancestral heartland of Kalimdor's quilboar.",sec={{t="Blood of the Boar God",b="Ten thousand years ago during the apocalyptic War of the Ancients, the colossal wild god Agamaggan threw himself into the fight against the Burning Legion. The great boar was eventually slain in battle, yet his sacrifice preserved life on Azeroth. Legends tell that wherever his blood seeped into the earth, massive thorn-covered vines erupted, forming thick, defensive labyrinths across the southern plains. The quilboar, venerating Agamaggan as their divine ancestor, claimed these colossal thickets as their holy lands, establishing the greatest of them as the Razorfen.",sp=0},{t="The Crone's Ambition",b="Razorfen Kraul is ruled with an iron tusk by the elder crone Charlga Razorflank. Under her despotic guidance, the shamanistic quilboar have abandoned their traditional territorial skirmishes to wage aggressive, coordinated war upon rival tribes, regional trade routes, and young Horde settlements. Far worse, troubling whispers and scout reports tell of undead fiends prowling near the brambles. It is feared that Charlga has begun negotiating with emissaries of the dreaded Scourge, seeking to harness forbidden necromancy to bolster her tribe's savagery.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Razorfen Kraul?",a="Razorfen Kraul is an ancient subterranean network of massive thorny vines in the Southern Barrens. It serves as the spiritual heartland and stronghold of the quilboar race, who consider the tangled labyrinth their ancestral home.",al={"what is rfk","explain razorfen kraul","razorfen overview"}},{q="How were the giant thorns created?",a="The enormous brambles sprouted from the earth ten thousand years ago during the War of the Ancients, springing forth directly from the blood spilled by the fallen boar demigod Agamaggan.",al={"why are there giant thorns","where did the brambles come from","agamaggan thorns"}},{q="Who rules Razorfen Kraul?",a="The Kraul is ruled by Charlga Razorflank, a ruthless quilboar crone and shaman who commands the Razorfen tribe and orchestrates attacks on neighboring villages and travelers.",al={"who is the boss of rfk","charlga razorflank","crone of the kraul"}},{q="Why is the Horde concerned about Razorfen Kraul?",a="Beyond constant quilboar raids on nascent settlements in the Barrens, Horde scouts have spotted undead skulking around the thickets, raising terrifying concerns that Charlga is aligning with the Scourge.",al={"why does the horde care","horde rfk interest","barrens threat"}},{q="Why are Alliance forces interested in the Kraul?",a="The aggressive expansion of Charlga's tribe threatens outposts near Feralas and the Thousand Needles, prompting Alliance commanders and scouts at Thalanaar to seek the crone's demise to stabilize the border.",al={"alliance quests rfk","why alliance go here","thalanaar quest"}},{q="What does defeating Earthcaller Halmgar mean for the story?",a="Defeating Earthcaller Halmgar, a rare and influential geomancer deep within the thickets, strikes a blow against the quilboar's earth-shaping priesthood. Stripping the Kraul of such powerful elemental summoners disrupts Charlga Razorflank's defensive fortifications and hinders the quilboar's ability to manipulate the sacred brambles of Agamaggan.",al={"what happens after earthcaller halmgar dies","earthcaller halmgar lore","halmgar defeated"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="The quilboar have long contested Mulgore's borders, and their desecration of the earth through dark alliances makes the cleansing of the Kraul a vital matter of tribal defense.",["class:Shaman"]="Quilboar geomancy twists the earth and elements around the blood of Agamaggan, providing a stark look at primal shamanistic powers wielded with savage intent.",["faction:Horde"]="Neutralizing the aggression within the Kraul is essential to protecting supply wagons and fledgling settlements across the southern expanses of the Barrens.",["race:Undead"]="Apothecaries from the Undercity take an acute interest in the bizarre reagents, bat guano, and rumors of Scourge incursions found within the briars."},kw={"agamaggan","barrens","charlga","halmgar","kraul","quilboar","ramtusk","razorfen","razorflank","scourge"},rel={"topic:agamaggan","topic:quilboar","topic:razorfen","npc:charlga-razorflank","npc:overlord-ramtusk","quest:1101","subzone:great-lift","subzone:thalanaar"},m={levels="29-38"},src={"Razorfen Kraul (Classic)","Razorfen Kraul"}}
